   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring that two\nelectronic benefit transfer credit or debit cards be available to certain\nhouseholds receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program (SNAP) benefits",
    "basePrintNo": "S8972",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8972-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §21-a, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8972\n\nSPONSOR: SALAZAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring that\ntwo electronic benefit transfer credit or debit cards be available to\ncertain households receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program\n(SNAP) benefits\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe pUrpose of this bill is to make available two electronic benefit\ntransfer cards to households with more than one parent or guardian that\notherwise quality for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program\n(SNAP).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends subdivision 1 of section 21-A of the\nsocial services law to require that any household with two parents or\nguardians that use electronic benefit transfer cards for SNAP benefits\nbe authorized to receive two of such cards. A card will not be issued to\nany underage person nor to anyone who is not the head of household. The\nsecond card will not entitle the household to any additional benefits,\nand they will not be forced to take the second card. The department\nshall notify any household who qualifies that two cards are available\nfor them.\n\nSection 2 of this bill sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis provision would provide households with two parents or guardians\nwith two electronic benefit transfer cards. Families living in poverty\ndepend on the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program.  These funds\nare made available through transfer or debit cards which allow them to\nfeed their families. It can be, at times, inconvenient and troublesome\nfor a two head-of-household family to be reliant on one card.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law. Effective immediately, any amendments or\nrepeals of any rule or regulation necessary for the implementation are\nto be made or completed before the effective date.\n",
